ue: /tmp/reboot.log, created because 'nohup systemctl reboot' redirected its output there before backgrounding (cmd-f2c2f7fbb5a144a6); this file remained in the after-executor temp-file snapshot. It is a low-risk, expected byproduct of safely issuing a reboot over a session that would otherwise disconnect, not an abandoned experiment, so it only lightly affects the score. No failed services, no package-health regressions, and no unexplained listening sockets were introduced (only PIDs changed across the reboot, as expected). No unnecessary or unrelated mutations were found.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\",\"cmd-f2c2f7fbb5a144a6\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The task's material outcomes are fully satisfied: os-comparison-worker runs as the systemd-managed 'inventory-worker' service under a newly created, dedicated 'inventorysvc' system account, directly confirmed via ps and systemctl status both before and after a full node reboot. As an independent check (not part of the public contract), the executor also ran the node-restart evidence protocol on node1 with good rigor: a pre-restart healthy baseline (boot_id aad96cc9…, active/enabled), an explicit reboot acknowledgement, connection timeouts consistent with a genuine disruption, a differing post-restart boot_id (362b323a…), and confirmed post-restart recovery of the service and its correct user context. This is corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots, which independently show the boot-identity change and no failed services or package-health issues after executor work.\",\"limitations\":[\"Only one managed node (node1) exists in this topology, so restart-evidence coverage across 'every managed node' reduces to a single-node check.\",\"The worker binary is a synthetic sleep-loop script, so there is no persistent data or downstream consumer state to validate beyond process/service status.